WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:07.779
The "Mortal Kombat" series is known for infamously
violent fatalities and a deep roster of badass

00:00:07.779 --> 00:00:10.657
fighters from realms across the multiverse.

00:00:10.657 --> 00:00:14.191
Translating these fighting games into movies
is no easy task.

00:00:14.191 --> 00:00:19.730
Here are the five best and five worst scenes
in 2021's "Mortal Kombat."

00:00:19.730 --> 00:00:25.019
"Mortal Kombat" puts its best foot forward
in an opening that takes place centuries before

00:00:25.019 --> 00:00:26.118
the rest of the movie.

00:00:26.118 --> 00:00:30.533
Sub-Zero comes to Hanzo Hasashi's home to
assassinate him and his family.

00:00:30.533 --> 00:00:36.510
After seeing his son and wife killed and frozen
by the cryomancer, Hanzo goes on a rampage,

00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:40.921
tearing through a legion of assassins with
his iconic Kunai rope.

00:00:40.921 --> 00:00:43.914
This leads to an epic showdown between the
two.

00:00:43.914 --> 00:00:48.350
The actors playing the iconic "Mortal Kombat"
duo - Joe Taslim and Hiroyuki Sanada - are

00:00:48.350 --> 00:00:51.120
veterans of martial arts and samurai cinema.

00:00:51.120 --> 00:00:57.030
The bouts between them are by far the highlight
of the 2021 "Mortal Kombat" adaptation, and

00:00:57.030 --> 00:01:00.456
the first one gets the movie off to a rousing
start.

00:01:00.456 --> 00:01:05.480
Sub-Zero walks away the victor, leaving Hanzo
dead as the screen fades to black and the

00:01:05.480 --> 00:01:06.790
title card fades in.

00:01:06.790 --> 00:01:09.413
It's time for "Mortal Kombat."

00:01:09.413 --> 00:01:15.704
A strength of the latest "Mortal Kombat" is
the direction and choreography of its hand-to-hand combat.

00:01:15.704 --> 00:01:20.469
Unfortunately, this means the scenes where
the actors have to fight against a CGI opponent

00:01:20.469 --> 00:01:25.673
stick out like a sore thumb amid the visually
superior physical action.

00:01:25.673 --> 00:01:30.930
The worst of these is a warehouse fight where
Cole, Sonya Blade, and Kano face off against

00:01:30.930 --> 00:01:33.166
an invisible human-sized reptile.

00:01:33.166 --> 00:01:37.604
Seeing the actors fight against air definitely
breaks the believability of the scene.

00:01:37.604 --> 00:01:42.400
When their adversary is invisible, the effects
aren't convincing enough to give you a solid

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:46.819
sense of its scope or location; when we do
get a glimpse, it still doesn't seem like

00:01:46.819 --> 00:01:48.773
much more than a generic beast.

00:01:48.773 --> 00:01:53.870
Once Kano punctures the lizard with a flare,
he becomes a whole lot easier to see and well...

00:01:53.870 --> 00:01:55.324
you know what's coming next.

00:01:55.324 --> 00:02:00.111
Still, even when the cast isn't punching at
nothing, the scene doesn't manage to excite.

00:02:00.111 --> 00:02:04.277
The special effects on the lizard don't look
especially stylish or cool.

00:02:04.277 --> 00:02:08.049
The end result is the most forgettable fight
of the entire movie.

00:02:08.049 --> 00:02:12.660
Eagle-eyed "Mortal Kombat" fans undoubtedly
noticed from trailers that early on in the

00:02:12.660 --> 00:02:17.550
movie Jax is lacking his defining characteristic
- his two cyborg arms.

00:02:17.550 --> 00:02:23.207
It doesn't take long for the movie to show
the traumatic incident that caused Jax's epic transformation.

00:02:23.207 --> 00:02:27.460
The early scenes where Jax has both his human
arms can be interpreted as a nod to "Mortal

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:30.000
Kombat II," the game where the character made
his debut.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:35.055
In the 2021 "Mortal Kombat ” Sub-Zero is
the one responsible for Jax's dismemberment.

00:02:35.055 --> 00:02:40.590
After hunting down Jax, Cole, and his family,
Sub-Zero lures Jax into battle.

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:45.640
The two have an intense combat session that
leads to a pretty gnarly time for Jax when

00:02:45.640 --> 00:02:51.627
Sub-Zero freezes his arms until they explode
into a bloody mess of ice and viscera.

00:02:51.627 --> 00:02:55.740
In the middle of the film, Liu Kang finds
Cole, Sonya, and Jax in the desert and the

00:02:55.740 --> 00:02:58.480
movie decides the real plot should start now.

00:02:58.480 --> 00:03:02.540
The legendary protector takes the crew to
Raiden's temple where the Earthrealm protectors

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.807
have the entire backstory of "Mortal Kombat"
and Outworld explained to them.

00:03:06.807 --> 00:03:11.514
Liu Kang tells the protectors about the tournament
and that's kind of his role for the entire movie.

00:03:11.514 --> 00:03:17.030
It is a major letdown to have the main hero
of a majority of the "Mortal Kombat" series

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:22.460
relegated to doling out exposition and training
the characters that actually get to fight.

00:03:22.460 --> 00:03:28.090
In less than 10 minutes of its total runtime,
"Mortal Kombat" introduces three major characters

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:30.620
and sets up the conflict for the rest of the
adventure.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:37.866
It's a rushed scene full of exposition that
reiterates information that most "Mortal Kombat" fans already know.

00:03:37.866 --> 00:03:43.100
Despite being squeezed between two action
sequences, this scene still manages to kill

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.796
the momentum in the middle of the movie.

00:03:45.796 --> 00:03:51.140
Cole unlocks his true potential when the four-armed
Goro is about to kill his family.

00:03:51.140 --> 00:03:56.990
With wife Alison and daughter Emily in harm's
way, Cole taps into his arcana, his body turning

00:03:56.990 --> 00:04:01.649
into an energy-absorbing armor not unlike
the "Black Panther" costume.

00:04:01.649 --> 00:04:07.220
Sure, the CGI-heavy fights in "Mortal Kombat"
aren't the best, but the final moments of

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:09.726
this sequence more than make up for that.

00:04:09.726 --> 00:04:15.660
When tapping into his power, Cole materializes
his weapons and proceeds to absolutely go

00:04:15.660 --> 00:04:17.196
to town on Goro.

00:04:17.196 --> 00:04:21.380
Only one of Cole's weapons is bladed, but
it definitely feels like they're an homage

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.000
to Tanya's in "Mortal Kombat: Deception" and
"Armageddon."

00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:32.330
Kano is the ultimate loudmouth and this scene
is him at his swear-iest, angriest, and most

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:33.615
overtly racist.

00:04:33.615 --> 00:04:39.970
Kano exudes machismo and spews some serious
anti-Asian sentiments as Kung Lao and Liu

00:04:39.970 --> 00:04:43.199
Kang egg him on to try and see his true power.

00:04:43.199 --> 00:04:47.409
It's only then that we see Kano's laser eye
in action for the first time in the movie.

00:04:47.409 --> 00:04:52.960
The scene goes way overboard on how offensive
Kano acts to the point where it begins to

00:04:52.960 --> 00:04:55.210
give away the twist that happens later on.

00:04:55.210 --> 00:04:58.090
There's no way you are supposed to root for
Kano after this.

00:04:58.090 --> 00:05:02.999
If it wasn't obvious Kano was destined to
betray the protectors to Shang Tsung, this

00:05:02.999 --> 00:05:07.550
scene makes it painfully clear that he is
not a good guy.

00:05:07.550 --> 00:05:12.300
Fighting games are known for creating some
of the biggest character rivalries in gaming,

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:15.449
and Sonya and Kano go way back as storied
rivals.

00:05:15.449 --> 00:05:22.110
Additionally, fans of the original 1995 movie
are sure to be reminded of the pair's classic face-off.

00:05:22.110 --> 00:05:26.960
The new movie leans hard into Kano being a
foul-mouthed scumbag.

00:05:26.960 --> 00:05:29.909
He's always been known for being cunning and
untrustworthy.

00:05:29.909 --> 00:05:35.259
The latest portrayal of Kano is no different,
as he betrays Sonya and the heroes of Earthrealm

00:05:35.259 --> 00:05:40.226
by removing the shield of protection around
the Raiden's temple - betraying Sonya's trust most of all.

00:05:40.226 --> 00:05:45.490
This relationship makes the final showdown
between the two supremely satisfying.

00:05:45.490 --> 00:05:51.060
When Sonya finally unleashes her garden gnome-based
fatality on Kano, she earns her dragon mark

00:05:51.060 --> 00:05:55.615
and finally becomes the protector of Earthrealm
she was destined to be.

00:05:55.615 --> 00:06:00.610
Not long after the protectors make it to Raiden's
temple, Sonya discovers Jax is alive and being

00:06:00.610 --> 00:06:02.669
cybernetically enhanced.

00:06:02.669 --> 00:06:06.180
As he recovers, Jax struggles with getting
accustomed to his new body.

00:06:06.180 --> 00:06:11.189
Thankfully Sonya is there to give a motivational
speech that works wonders for Jax, but leaves

00:06:11.189 --> 00:06:12.969
the audience a bit cold.

00:06:12.969 --> 00:06:18.889
The attempt to develop this crucial "Mortal
Kombat" relationship is a bit "too little too late."

00:06:18.889 --> 00:06:23.919
While Sonya and Jax are indeed partners and
have a close friendship in the games and comics

00:06:23.919 --> 00:06:27.449
lore, the connection doesn't come across as
well in the newest movie.

00:06:27.449 --> 00:06:31.809
Sonya's words of motivation clue into the
duo's military background together, but the

00:06:31.809 --> 00:06:37.286
monologue doesn't land on an emotional level
and falls flat as the movie barrels forward.

00:06:37.286 --> 00:06:42.580
In the biggest twist of the whole movie, Cole's
ancestor warps back from the depths of the

00:06:42.580 --> 00:06:46.229
Netherrealm to finally defeat Sub-Zero once
and for all.

00:06:46.229 --> 00:06:51.210
Right before Sub-Zero is about to deal a death
blow to Cole, Hanzo's Kunai lodges its way

00:06:51.210 --> 00:06:55.800
into his arm before the ancient hero lets
loose his iconic battle cry.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:07:01.568
It wouldn't be a "Mortal Kombat" movie without
at least one "get over here," now would it?

00:07:01.568 --> 00:07:03.816
"Get over here!"

00:07:03.816 --> 00:07:10.259
It is once again worth mentioning how fantastic
the action and choreography are in the scenes

00:07:10.259 --> 00:07:12.972
featuring these two martial arts film stars.

00:07:12.972 --> 00:07:19.150
The climactic action sequence fully delivers
on being one of the best in the movie, featuring

00:07:19.150 --> 00:07:22.819
weapons, fists, and magic powers in equal
measure.

00:07:22.819 --> 00:07:28.389
Hanzo fully makes the transition to Scorpion
and finishes Sub-Zero with the fire breath

00:07:28.389 --> 00:07:33.304
fatality "Mortal Kombat" fans remember from
way back in the day at the arcades.

00:07:33.304 --> 00:07:37.729
It is hard to top the climactic battle between
Scorpion and Sub-Zero, but "Mortal Kombat"

00:07:37.729 --> 00:07:42.535
wraps up so quickly and abruptly it's hard
not to feel like you fell asleep or missed something.

00:07:42.535 --> 00:07:47.139
Of the final scenes, the one that feels most
rushed is the confrontation between the leaders

00:07:47.139 --> 00:07:51.259
of each realm: thunder god Lord Raiden versus
the evil Shang Tsung.

00:07:51.259 --> 00:07:55.562
It ends up being less of a confrontation and
more of a short conversation.

00:07:55.562 --> 00:08:00.020
After it becomes clear that Raiden and the
forces of Earthrealm have defeated their Outworld

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:04.878
foes, Shang Tsung teleports into the scene
to tell the heroes the fight is not over yet.

00:08:04.878 --> 00:08:09.319
He swears he will get his revenge, and then
it looks like Raiden is preparing to battle

00:08:09.319 --> 00:08:10.930
in one last epic fight.

00:08:10.930 --> 00:08:13.140
But that is ... not what happens.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:17.819
Instead, Raiden uses a lightning blast to
send Shang Tsung back to Outworld, buying

00:08:17.819 --> 00:08:20.433
time to gather more allies for the sequel.

